{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nEighteen `tests/unit` modules contain 36 audited prose blocks: 28 leading docstrings and 8 full-line comment regions (4,108 before-words), frozen at `origin/main@d6669496cae441fc8381b5ee6de21a3993defd84`. Revalidation split the composite `conftest.py` range, removed two stale ranges that now contain executable code, and pruned the already-concise `classify` rationale.\n\n## Approach\nEdit only the frozen prose blocks below. A `D:<owner>` is the leading `Expr(Constant(str))` in a `Module`, `ClassDef`, `FunctionDef`, or `AsyncFunctionDef`. A `C:<scope>:before:<anchor>` is one maximal consecutive full-line COMMENT-token region, owned by the innermost AST scope and anchored to the next unchanged non-comment code. Compact `D{a,b}` and `C{scope@anchor,...}` notation expands to those exact IDs under the row's path; the reviewer writes the fully path-qualified `<path>#<ID>`.\n\nFor every owned path, retain immutable before and final blobs and parse both with `ast.parse(..., type_comments=True)`. On comparison copies remove only allowlisted leading docstring nodes; normalize only `ast.TypeIgnore.lineno`; require the remaining `ast.dump(..., include_attributes=False)` values to match. Tokenize both blobs and reject changed inline comments or non-allowlisted full-line comments. Preserve runtime strings, regexes, prompts, imports, decorators, annotations, assertions, subprocess arguments, test data, shebangs, and complete directive-bearing physical lines exactly. Only adjacent blank-line normalization around an edited block is allowed.\n\n## Stable block allowlist\n- `tests/unit/_opcert_helpers.py` — `D{<module>,store_with_chain}`\n- `tests/unit/conftest.py` — `D{<module>,_no_real_session_log_writes,_isolated_mcp_client_home,_isolated_aws_provider_credentials}`; `C{<module>@_ENGINE_PKG_DIR,_bridge_reconciler_shadow_package@_front}`\n- `tests/unit/gold_set_completion.py` — `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_8d44_cache_attestation_freshness.py` — `D:<module>`; `C{test_reduce_reflects_ondisk_attestation_after_stale_cache@warm,test_reduce_reflects_ondisk_attestation_after_stale_cache@cache,test_reduce_reflects_ondisk_attestation_after_stale_cache@state}`\n- `tests/unit/test_a8e5_absence_veto_edge.py` — `D:test_f1fa_1144_false_absence_regression_fixture`\n- `tests/unit/test_ac_satisfiability_criterion.py` — `D{<module>,test_routing_entry,test_reaches_pass1_and_attributes}`\n- `tests/unit/test_administrative_close_dispositions.py` — `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_advanced_cli_parsers.py` — `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_agent_call_memo_nudge.py` — `D:<module>`; `C{<module>@def _file_backed_read_file}`\n- `tests/unit/test_agent_call_runaway_guard_c827.py` — `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_agent_call_seam.py` — `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_agent_skill_ticket_workflow_guidance.py` — `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_agentic_budget_and_truncation.py` — `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_agentic_message_cache.py` — `D{<module>,test_agentic_anthropic_adds_the_automatic_message_breakpoint,test_captured_agentic_request_carries_a_breakpoint_after_the_message_history,test_the_anthropic_breakpoint_budget_is_not_exceeded_on_the_agentic_path}`\n- `tests/unit/test_agents_claim_assignee_guidance.py` — `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_agents_serena_untyped_receiver.py` — `D:<module>`; `C{test_nav_doc_carries_the_untyped_receiver_reproduction@assert \"dispatch_one.py\" in doc}`\n- `tests/unit/test_alarm_actions_terraform.py` — `D{<module>,_rendered_description}`; `C{<module>@_MIN_EXPECTED_ALARMS}`\n- `tests/unit/test_amend_msg_change_id.py` — `D:<module>`\n\n## Protected false positives\nAll unlisted prose is protected, including `conftest.py`'s `classify` comment and `_isolated_aws_home` docstring, concise helper/test docstrings, `test_agentic_message_cache.py`'s old 259–261 non-prose span, and `test_alarm_actions_terraform.py`'s old 422–427 non-prose span. Inside the alarm module docstring, preserve the literal `# rebar:allow-actionless-alarm: <reason>` and `# rebar:allow-missing-data-notbreaching: <reason>` examples exactly.\n\n## Preserved contracts and consumers\nKeep op-cert ordering; hermetic import/session/MCP/AWS fixtures; frozen completion labels; disk-fresh attestation reduction; absence and satisfiability routing; close/parser/agent-call/memo/runaway/budget/cache/assignee/Serena contracts; alarm action, missing-data, anti-vacuity and AWS-length rules; and Change-Id/sign-off preservation. Direct test consumers include the op-cert helper importers, `test_completion_floor_e2e.py`, `test_gate_scratch_volume_aa40.py`, and `test_bedrock_provider.py`; the calibration script imports the gold set. No allowlisted target has a `__doc__`, `inspect.getdoc`, or pydoc consumer.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Prose changes occur only inside the 36 declared stable-ID blocks.\n- [ ] Any changed blank line is adjacent to an edited stable-ID block.\n- [ ] The normalized-AST comparison passes on every owned path.\n- [ ] The token/comment comparison passes on every owned path.\n- [ ] A non-author reviewer posts exactly 36 leaf-linked TSV rows, one for each declared stable-ID block.\n- [ ] Every reviewer row uses this schema: stable_block_id<TAB>before_citation<TAB>final_citation<TAB>preserved_contract_or_consumer<TAB>directives_exact<TAB>before_words<TAB>after_words<TAB>semantic-preservation<TAB>bloat-removal<TAB>reviewer_session.\n- [ ] Every before_citation equals d6669496cae441fc8381b5ee6de21a3993defd84:<path>#<stable-id>.\n- [ ] Every final_citation equals <final-commit-sha>:<path>#<stable-id>.\n- [ ] Every row records after_words < before_words.\n- [ ] Every row records directives_exact=PASS.\n- [ ] Every row records semantic-preservation=PASS, confirming its preserved_contract_or_consumer.\n- [ ] Every row records bloat-removal=PASS, confirming removal of chronology, duplication, obvious narration, or separator ornament.\n- [ ] All five structured verify commands pass.\n## Verification\nThe five DD-level commands recorded on this ticket run focused pytest with real consumers, scoped Ruff check plus format-check, comment hygiene, owned-path `git diff --check`, and worktree-venv `make verify`. They are the executable completion oracle."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788663487278452001,"uuid":"ebc45431-7fee-42d6-aa02-3af7a58580e8"}